leone">Sierra Leone</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1824</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maccarthy">MacCarthy</a> is killed and most of his force wiped out in a battle with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a> forces; a British, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fante">Fante</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a> force defeats an Asante invasion of the coast in 1826.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1844</span><span class="rf-text">Commander Henry Worsley Hill negotiates the Bond of 1844 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fante">Fante</a> and other chiefs, who submit murder and robbery to British jurisdiction.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1874</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garnet-wolseley">Sir Garnet Wolseley</a>'s force occupies and burns <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a> in January; the coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> is proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> Colony on 24 July.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1896</span><span class="rf-text">A second British expedition occupies <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a>, makes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a> a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and exiles the asantehene.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1902</span><span class="rf-text">After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-golden-stool">War of the Golden Stool</a> of 1900 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a> is proclaimed a colony and the Northern Territories a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> under the governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>.</span></l